$\cos A=n \cos B$ and $\sin A=m \sin B$

Squaring and adding, we get $1=n^{2} \cos ^{2} B+m^{2} \sin ^{2} B$

$$

\begin{array}{ll}

\Rightarrow & 1=n^{2}\left(1-\sin ^{2} B\right)+m^{2} \sin ^{2} B \\

\therefore & \left(m^{2}-n^{2}\right) \sin ^{2} B=1-n^{2}

\end{array}

$$
